{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.exists_collision_earlier_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.exists_collision_earlier_col","kind":"theorem","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L422-L438","doc":"**The row collision.** Strengthening of `exists_sameRow_earlier_col` to what the\nGarnir annihilation actually consumes: with `c < c'` strict, the colliding label `x`\nis *distinct* from `s` (their columns differ), so `swap x s` is a genuine same-row\ntransposition of `C ∪ {s}`.\n\nThis is the collision for `t` itself; the version needed inside\n`sum_sign_rep_polytabloid_eq_zero_of_family` is for `ρ • t` with `ρ ∈ colStab t`, which\n`colPattern_smul_of_mem_colStab` reduces to this one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.exists_sameRow_earlier_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.exists_sameRow_earlier_col","kind":"theorem","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L384-L419","doc":"**The colliding label exists (steps 2–4 of the row collision, in one).** For any\ntableau `t`, if `s` sits in column `c'` and `c ≤ c'`, then some label `x` sits in\ncolumn `c` *in the same row as `s`*.\n\nThe bean's plan routed this through \"the column-`c` labels occupy exactly rows\n`0 … colLen c − 1`\". That intermediate is unnecessary: a tableau is an `Equiv` onto\n`μ.cells`, so it suffices to show the *cell* `(row s, c)` is in `μ` and then pull it\nback. Concretely, with `r = row s`:\n\n* `(r, c') ∈ μ` gives `r < colLen c'` (`mem_iff_lt_colLen`);\n* `colLen c' ≤ colLen c` since `c ≤ c'` (`colLen_anti`) — columns weakly shorten;\n* so `r < colLen c`, i.e. `(r, c) ∈ μ`;\n* `t.symm` on that cell is the required `x`.\n\nNo column-superstandardness, no counting — this is generic in `t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.colLabels_smul_of_mem_colStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.colLabels_smul_of_mem_colStab","kind":"theorem","line":371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L371-L381","doc":"**The column-`c` label set is `colStab`-invariant.** Immediate from\n`colPattern_smul_of_mem_colStab`: the labels sitting in column `c` of `ρ • t` are\nexactly those sitting in column `c` of `t`.\n\nThis is the form the collision consumes — the Garnir set `C` is defined from `t`, but\nthe tabloid-level vanishing must be checked in `ρ • t` for every `ρ ∈ colStab t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.colPattern_smul_of_mem_colStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.colPattern_smul_of_mem_colStab","kind":"theorem","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L357-L368","doc":"**A column-stabiliser element preserves the column pattern.** For `ρ ∈ colStab t`,\n`ρ • t` has literally the same column pattern as `t` — this is `mem_colStab` read\nthrough the equivariance `colPattern_smul`.\n\nFirst step of the brick-3b row collision: it is what makes \"the column-`c` labels of\n`ρ • t` are still exactly the column-`c` labels of `t`\" true, so the collision argument\nmay reason about `C` in `t` while the tabloid lives over `ρ • t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.jm_polytabloid_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.jm_polytabloid_split","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L312-L331","doc":"**The JM sum, split by column** (brick 1 + brick 3a). The JM action on `e_t`\nis `(same-column count) · (−e_t)` plus the **off-column** sum\n`Σ_{j<s, swap j s ∉ colStab t} e_{(j s)·t}`. This isolates the off-column\n(Garnir) part as the sole remaining piece of the eigen-equation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.sameColumn_sum_polytabloid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.sameColumn_sum_polytabloid","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L295-L310","doc":"**Same-column contribution.** The same-column part of the JM polytabloid sum\n(`j < s` with `swap j s ∈ colStab t`) is `(count) · (−e_t)` — each term is\n`−e_t` by `polytabloid_swap_colStab`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.colGarnir_single_column_of_annihilation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.colGarnir_single_column_of_annihilation","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L258-L284","doc":"**Single-column Garnir relation from the full-group annihilation (sorry-free,\nconditional).** Over a characteristic-zero field, once the full-group\nannihilation `∑_{σ∈S_{C∪{s}}} sgn(σ)·σ·e_t = 0` is known, the coset factorisation\n`colGarnir_fullgroup_sum` gives `|S_C|·(e_t − ∑_{j∈C} e_{(j\\,s)·t}) = 0`, and\ndividing by `|S_C| = |C|! ≠ 0` yields the single-column relation\n`∑_{j∈C} e_{(j\\,s)·t} = e_t`. This isolates the **only** remaining debt of brick 3b\nas the annihilation itself (the collision-dependent piece). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.colGarnir_fullgroup_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.colGarnir_fullgroup_sum","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L150-L253","doc":"**The full-group single-column Garnir sum = `|S_C| · (e_t − ∑ e_{(j\\,s)·t})`\n(sorry-free, collision-independent).** For a label set `C` lying in one column of\n`t` (hypothesis `hCcol`: every permutation supported on `C` preserves columns) and\na label `s ∉ C`, the signed representation sum over the **full** group `S_{C∪{s}}`\nfactors as `|S_C|` copies of the outer star-sum. Route: reindex `S_{C∪{s}}` by the\nbijection `(x, π) ↦ (x\\,s)·π` onto `(C∪{s}) × S_C`, collapse the inner `S_C`-sum\nto `|S_C|·e_t` by column antisymmetry (`colStab_subset_sum_rep_polytabloid`), and\nrecognise the outer sum via `starSum_rep_polytabloid`. Combined with the\n(collision-dependent) full-group **annihilation** `= 0` and `|S_C| = |C|! ≠ 0`,\nthis yields the single-column relation `∑_{j∈C} e_{(j\\,s)·t} = e_t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.mem_permFixingOutside","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.mem_permFixingOutside","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L144-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.permFixingOutside","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.permFixingOutside","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L136-L141","doc":"The subgroup `S_D` of permutations fixing every label **outside** `D`\n(realised as a `Finset`), used as `S_C` and `S_{C∪{s}}` in the single-column\nGarnir coset decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.starSum_rep_polytabloid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.starSum_rep_polytabloid","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L103-L133","doc":"**The outer star-sum evaluation.** The signed transposition sum over the\n`|C|+1` coset representatives `{(x\\,s) : x ∈ {s} ∪ C}` (with `(s\\,s) = 1`)\nevaluates to `e_t − ∑_{j∈C} e_{(j\\,s)·t}`: the `x = s` term contributes `+e_t`\n(identity), and each `x = j ∈ C` term contributes `−e_{(j\\,s)·t}`\n(`sgn(swap j s) = −1`, `rep_polytabloid`). This is the RHS of the single-column\nGarnir cancellation `0 = |C|!·(e_t − ∑_{j∈C} e_{(j\\,s)·t})`; collision-independent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.colStab_subset_sum_rep_polytabloid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.colStab_subset_sum_rep_polytabloid","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L83-L101","doc":"**C-antisymmetry sum collapse (the coset-inner-sum).** For any finite set `H`\nof permutations all lying in the column stabilizer of `t`, the signed\nrepresentation sum collapses to `|H| · e_t`: each term is\n`sgn(σ) · (sgn(σ) · e_t) = sgn(σ)² · e_t = e_t` by brick 2\n(`rep_colStab_polytabloid`) and `sgn(σ)² = 1`. This is the inner sum over a\nfull-column subgroup `S_C ⊆ colStab t` in the coset decomposition of the\nsingle-column Garnir relation (brick 3b): it turns `∑_{π ∈ S_C} sgn(π)·π·e_t`\ninto `|C|! · e_t`. Collision-independent — pure column antisymmetry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.polytabloid_swap_colStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.polytabloid_swap_colStab","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L72-L81","doc":"**A same-column transposition negates the polytabloid.** If the transposition\n`swap j s` lies in the column stabilizer of `t` (i.e. `j, s` are in the same\ncolumn), then `e_{(j\\,s)·t} = − e_t` — the sign of a transposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.rep_colStab_polytabloid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.rep_colStab_polytabloid","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L47-L70","doc":"**Column antisymmetry.** For `σ` in the column stabilizer of `t`, permuting the\ncolumns signs the polytabloid: `rep σ (e_t) = sgn(σ) · e_t`. Reindex the\ncolumn-stabilizer sum by left-multiplication by `σ` (a bijection of `colStab t`,\nas `σ ∈ colStab t`); `sgn(σ·π) = sgn(σ)·sgn(π)` and `sgn(σ)² = 1` collapse the\nsigns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.jm_smul_polytabloid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OVBaseSeminormalVector.jm_smul_polytabloid","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OVBaseSeminormalVector.lean#L28-L43","doc":"**JM action on a polytabloid = a polytabloid sum.** The Jucys–Murphy element\n`X_s = ∑_{j<s} (j\\,s)` acts on the polytabloid `e_t` by\n`∑_{j<s} e_{(j\\,s)·t}` — each transposition permutes the polytabloid\n(`rep_polytabloid`), and `asAlgebraHom` sends the `single` sum to the\nendomorphism sum. General in `t`; the eigen-equation is what this sum collapses\nto for the column-superstandard `T₀`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}